      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the Queets River, whose Quinault word means “dirt” and reflects the tribe’s connection to the land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        29,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
