        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://unitedstatesghosttowns.com/queets-washington-ghost-town/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1880 a post office opened in Queets, operating until 1934 before mail was routed to nearby Clearwater.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queets%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The abandoned cannery buildings and former settler homes stand as silent reminders of Queets’ once‑bustling fishing community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://unitedstatesghosttowns.com/queets-washington-ghost-town/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Queets lies within Olympic National Park’s Queets Corridor, a 14‑mile strip preserving traditional hunting, ceremonial grounds, and ancient ritual sites.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
